From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:26:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] fix(wlan): make RX statistics opt-in and drop the ADDBA
 reject switch

The RX diagnostics are going into the shipped kernel. The two-second
ECHO_WLAN_RXSTAT summary and the rate-limited anomaly lines should not
reach a 921600-baud console (console loglevel 8) by default.

- rx_stat_period_ms (default 0): print ECHO_WLAN_RXSTAT every N ms
  (minimum 100) while frames arrive; 0 prints nothing. The counters
  always run, and enabling it re-arms the interval and resets the
  per-interval maxima, so the first summary covers one full period.
- The ECHO_WLAN_RXHIF and ECHO_WLAN_RX_BA anomaly lines (fall-ahead,
  fall-behind retry drop, BAR, timeout give-up, HIF length anomalies)
  go through ECHO_RX_LOG(): pr_info_ratelimited when rx_stat_period_ms
  is set, pr_debug_ratelimited otherwise.
- Remove rx_ba_reject. With CMD_ID_ADDBA_REJECT sent on association
  this firmware never completes association (stuck in ASSOCIATING).
  rx_ba_win stays.

  echo 2000 > /sys/module/wlan_mt/parameters/rx_stat_period_ms
